, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"description": "", "large_image": "6x37gz44HX9DRId6.png", "title": "Trump\u2019s $410 Million \u2018Office of Remigration\u2019 Has Deported Tens of Thousands of Migrants to \u2018Third Countries.\u2019"}, "post_flair_text": "DEPORT", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATVMGGjto", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 25, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8848688, "raw_content": "**UNITED NATIONS \u2022 NEW YORK**\r\n\r\n**President Trump Addresses the 81st United Nations General Assembly \u2014 Watch Live Tomorrow Morning**\r\n\r\nTomorrow, Tuesday, September 22, 2026, President Donald J. Trump will address world leaders at the opening of the General Debate of the 81st session of the United Nations General Assembly at U.N. Headquarters in New York City.\r\n\r\nThe morning session begins at 9:00 a.m. EDT. Brazilian President Luiz In\u00e1cio Lula da Silva is scheduled as the first speaker, followed by the President of the United States. Live coverage will stream on WhiteHouse.gov/live and the White House mobile app.\r\n\r\nDownload the app at whitehouse.gov/app/download to watch on iPhone or Android. Following the address, the President will hold a series of bilateral meetings in New York, including sessions with the Prime Minister of the United Kingdom and the Prime Minister of Japan, and will meet with leaders of the Gulf Cooperation Council before returning to Washington on Tuesday evening.\r\n\r\n**WATCH DETAILS**\r\n\r\nDate: Tuesday, September 22, 2026\r\n\r\nCoverage begins: 9:00 a.m. EDT\r\n\r\nLocation: United Nations Headquarters, New York\r\n\r\nSpeaking order: After Brazil; first day of the General Debate\r\n\r\nOfficial stream: WhiteHouse.gov/live\r\n\r\nMobile app: Stream on the White House app \u2014 whitehouse.gov/app/download", "author": "FreeFire", "created": 1790021309716, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "President Trump Addresses the 81st United Nations General Assembly \u2014 Watch Live Tomorrow Morning 9:00 a.m. EDT", "last_comment_created": 1790021309716, "content": "<p><strong>UNITED NATIONS \u2022 NEW YORK</strong></p>\n<p><strong>President Trump Addresses the 81st United Nations General Assembly \u2014 Watch Live Tomorrow Morning</strong></p>\n<p>Tomorrow, Tuesday, September 22, 2026, President Donald J. Trump will address world leaders at the opening of the General Debate of the 81st session of the United Nations General Assembly at U.N. Headquarters in New York City.</p>\n<p>The morning session begins at 9:00 a.m. EDT. Brazilian President Luiz In\u00e1cio Lula da Silva is scheduled as the first speaker, followed by the President of the United States. Live coverage will stream on WhiteHouse.gov/live and the White House mobile app.</p>\n<p>Download the app at whitehouse.gov/app/download to watch on iPhone or Android. Following the address, the President will hold a series of bilateral meetings in New York, including sessions with the Prime Minister of the United Kingdom and the Prime Minister of Japan, and will meet with leaders of the Gulf Cooperation Council before returning to Washington on Tuesday evening.</p>\n<p><strong>WATCH DETAILS</strong></p>\n<p>Date: Tuesday, September 22, 2026</p>\n<p>Coverage begins: 9:00 a.m. EDT</p>\n<p>Location: United Nations Headquarters, New York</p>\n<p>Speaking order: After Brazil; first day of the General Debate</p>\n<p>Official stream: WhiteHouse.gov/live</p>\n<p>Mobile app: Stream on the White House app \u2014 whitehouse.gov/app/download</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_t